 @THMTHERMO  That's the model I have as well. Got it in 2018 when the 20 series released which I originally wanted to get, but then was waaay too expensive. Paid 450€ for the 1080 then, it was basically new coming out of a prebuilt that someone bought as an upgrade who already had the 1080ti before. That exact thing was priced 600€ at the store he got his prebuilt from. Was a big W for both of us I guess...

I replaced that gigachad of a graphics card early 22 with an Asus 3070 featuring the Noctua cooler - which is now to be replaced by a 4080S with the same (or probably improved) Noctua Chungus Unit Of Cooling. 3070 with just 8GB doesn't cut it if you wanna run VR without lowering your resolution, at least when it comes to flight sims.

If it wasn't for VR, I'd very much probably still run that 1080...
